Copyright (c) 2026 Xaxis and the Blocklore contributors

The claims, topic layouts, digests, run logs, snapshots and other files in this
directory are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License. You may share and adapt them for any purpose, including commercially,
as long as you give appropriate credit, link to the license, and indicate if
changes were made. The full legal code is at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

How to credit a claim: name Blocklore, link the claim's own URL, and name the
license, for example:

    "Blocklore, https://blocklore.space/claims/<id>, CC BY 4.0"

What this license does not cover:

- Quotes. Each source in a claim carries a short quote (at most 50 words) from
  the cited work, included so anyone can check the claim against its source.
  Those quotes belong to their authors and stay under the terms of the work
  they come from. Reuse them as citations, with their source, or check that
  source's own license.
- Facts read from the Bitcoin blockchain, which belong to no one.
- Names and marks of third parties.

The software that produces and checks this store is MIT licensed: see LICENSE
at the root of the repository.
